    "body": "Hopefully fixes #7997 (although I didn't personally manage to reproduce the bug(s) either with or without it. Although I also suspect it's very intermittent).\r\n\r\nI don't think Cython itself is thread-safe (or easily made thread-safe, because there's lots of little bits of global state). Therefore I think the easiest solution is to run it in isolated processes when called in parallel by setuptools.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/cython/cython/pull/8008#discussion_r4075769009"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/pulls/8008"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/cython/cython/pulls/comments/4075769009"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "My alternative thought was to not have the `force_parallel` parameter but instead do\n\n```\nnthreads = 0 if threading.current_thread() is threading.main_thread() else 1\n```\n\nThat makes it less `setuptools`-specific (although I think most other uses are driven from the command-line where this is less of an issue) but a little more \"magic-special-case\".",
            "commit_id": "a0ccaf83e1fe3c07cc3783e3fb0ca8363e1fb02d",
            "created_at": "2026-09-22T19:48:13Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -1132,7 +1136,7 @@ def file_in_build_dir(c_file):\n     ]\n \n     if N <= 1:\n-        nthreads = 0\n+        nthreads = 1 if force_parallel else 0",
